<p class="xmsonormal">Brian,<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">Got some questions fired at me for the STA 360 estimate, see responses below.&nbsp; I&#8217;m sure you&#8217;ll have more, feel free to give me a call.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">Also &#8211; Working with Siemens on the breaker estimate, they gave a +/-30% estimate at 300k each.&nbsp; That would be for the breaker, frame, disconnects, PTs, relays, and battery.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">Questions from ES Estimating Group as the PM team has requested a revised estimate based on the most recent scope :<o:p></o:p></p>
<p class="xmsonormal">Please check the dollar amount below, all from previous estimate E-23-373.<o:p></o:p></p>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Battery System - $12,106,850.&nbsp;
<o:p></o:p></li><ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo1">Assuming this is the DC Battery for Control this will be captured in the Breaker estimate<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Transportation/Spare Parts - $585,688.<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="2" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo2">unknown<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="3" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Battery labor - $2,553,828, 16,801 mhrs is this for the entire new SS or just for the batteries?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="3" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo3">Not sure what this is<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="4" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">PCS Units - $832,022 is this for the batteries or is this the cost for the five outdoor standalone feeder cabinets?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="4" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo4">Not sure what this is &#8211; may be a carry over for the PCS for the BESS<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="5" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Step up transformers - $630,371.<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="5" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo5">Is this Station Service Transformers or GSUs?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="6" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Site Sound Mitigation - $466,766 - is this done? Do I need to include the estimate?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="6" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo6">I would carry this as a risk item if its needed or not<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="7" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1">Rental - Spot Generator - $139,700 - Did not see in scope but is included in est. E-23-373, Include in Est. or not?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="7" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l1 level2 lfo7">I don&#8217;t this this is needed &#8211; we are going to put station service transforms in first so we should be good<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<p class="xmsonormal">Other questions:<o:p></o:p></p>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo8">Is it an overhead cable or bus from the wood riser pole to the Siemens Breaker? Size and length?<o:p></o:p></li><ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level2 lfo8">Overhead cable -25&#8217; per phase should cover us on both sides of the breaker<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo8">The three SSVT pad mount transformers, I added three riser structures with foundations. Also add UG cable, 500LF per SSVT.&nbsp; Let me know if you agree with this.<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="2" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level2 lfo9">Should be down to 1 Station Service Transformer pad mount.&nbsp; 500&#8217; is plenty<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="3" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo8">On the eight wood riser poles, are the breaker disconnect switches located on these poles?<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="3" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level2 lfo10">Breaker Disconnects are on the skid for the breaker<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="4" type="1">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level1 lfo8">PTs (8 locations each side of the Siemens breaker, 24 total) - are they installed on the wood riser poles? or on their own steel supports?
<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="4" type="1">
<ol style="margin-top:0in" start="1" type="a">
<li class="xmsonormal" style="mso-list:l0 level2 lfo11">PTs are on the breaker skid<o:p></o:p></li></ol>
</ol>
